# Erudite Wizard: "Whenever you draw your second card each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature" (CR 121.2, 603.2). "Each turn" is every
# turn, not only Bot1's: on turn 2 Bot2's Ancestral Recall makes Bot1 draw three, its first three cards that turn, and the second of them gives one
# counter (the third none). On turn 3 the count starts again: the draw step's card is the first, and no more counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Erudite Wizard
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Ancestral Recall
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Erudite Wizard.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 8
? Bot1.Battlefield.Erudite Wizard.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Erudite Wizard.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Erudite Wizard.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Erudite Wizard.Toughness = 4
